# DR-0015: Select All Supervised Candidates Deterministically in Loop 1

## Status

Accepted

## Context

Loop 1 has a complete candidate tile catalog containing:

```text
total candidates: 870
positive candidates: 19
negative-only candidates: 31
all-ignore candidates: 820
```

The project must convert this complete candidate population into an explicit supervised sampling selection.

The selection policy must preserve the label semantics:

```text
POSITIVE = 1
NEGATIVE = 0
IGNORE = 255
```

In particular:

```text
UNLABELED != NEGATIVE
```

An all-ignore candidate contains no supervised pixels and must not enter supervised training merely because it contains no positive pixels.

Loop 1 is intentionally small, real, and complete. It is not intended to optimize class balance or reduce the eligible population before a baseline model exists.

## Decision

Loop 1 selects every candidate containing at least one supervised pixel.

The approved policy is:

```text
select all eligible candidates: true
exclude all-ignore candidates: true
selection order: candidate catalog order
hard-negative handling: require source provenance
```

Eligibility is determined as follows:

```text
supervised_pixel_count > 0
    -> eligible

supervised_pixel_count = 0
    -> ineligible
```

No random sampling, class balancing, down-sampling, or hard-negative prioritization is performed in Loop 1.

